      "generated_answer": "Clovis points are associated with some of the earliest well-documented human cultures in North America, dating to around 13,000 years ago. They are widely found throughout the continental United States, Mexico, and parts of Canada, but not in Alaska, where different tool traditions (such as those linked to the Nenana and Denali complexes) are present. This suggests human migration patterns and technological differences in far northern regions.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
