      "generated_answer": "The location of the foramen magnum, the hole in the skull where the spinal cord passes, indicates whether a primate is a biped or quadruped. In bipeds, it is positioned toward the bottom of the skull, allowing the spine to align centrally under the skull for upright posture, whereas in quadrupeds it is positioned more posteriorly. This anatomical feature is a key indicator of locomotor habit.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
