      "generated_answer": "The passage reflects the spirit of unity among Asian and African nations seeking to remain independent of the superpower blocs during the Cold War. Sukarno's emphasis on peace, moral strength, and collective action by 1.4 billion people from Asia and Africa aligns with the principles of the Non-Aligned Movement. This movement was formally established in 1961, but its foundations were laid at the 1955 Bandung Conference.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
