    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The rising literacy rates from 1897 to 1955 were particularly transformative for groups that previously had limited access to education. In late Imperial Russia and the early Soviet period, the rural peasantry constituted the largest illiterate population, and Soviet educational reforms specifically targeted rural areas to eliminate illiteracy. Therefore, the rural peasantry would have benefited most from these improvements.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
