      "generated_answer": "The development and application of steam-powered technologies (G) contributed least to Western European global hegemony between 1450 and 1750, as steam power became significant only during the Industrial Revolution in the late 18th century. The other options, such as naval technology, colonization, joint-stock companies, and gunpowder, were key factors within the specified time frame. Thus, steam technology was not yet a factor in European dominance during this period.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
