      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}\n\nThe Zenger case established an important precedent for freedom of the press by affirming the right to publish the truth as a defense against charges of seditious libel. This aligns most closely with the Pentagon Papers case, where the government attempted to block the publication of classified information, and the Supreme Court ruled in favor of the press’s right to publish. Both cases center on the press’s role in exposing government actions and upholding public accountability.",
