      "generated_answer": "B. Yes, because the tariff promoted industrial justice\n\nThe Underwood-Simmons Tariff of 1913 lowered tariffs, which Progressives supported as a step toward reducing the power of big businesses and promoting fairer economic conditions. Since the Progressive Party Platform emphasized industrial justice and using government to serve the public welfare, they would likely endorse this tariff reform. \n\n\\boxed{B}",
