      "generated_answer": "The Carlsbad Resolutions were designed to suppress liberal and nationalist movements that threatened the existing monarchies in Europe. As part of Metternich's conservative policies, they aimed to censor the press and prevent revolutionary ideas from spreading. This aligns most closely with suppressing nationalist revolutions.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
