    "global index": "MMLUPro_history_4609",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This question refers to the following information.\n\"The question as to who, and what, is responsible for African underdevelopment can be answered at two levels. Firstly, the answer is that the operation of the imperialist system bears major responsibility for African economic retardation by draining African wealth and by making it impossible to develop more rapidly the resources of the continent. Secondly, one has to deal with those who manipulate the system and those who are either agents or unwitting accomplices of the said system. The capitalists of Western Europe were the ones who actively extended their exploitation from inside Europe to cover the whole of Africa.\"\nWalter Rodney, historian, How Europe Underdeveloped Africa, 1974\nRodney's argument in the passage is most likely a response to which of the following developments of the period 1450 to 1750 C.E.?\n\nOptions: \nA. The colonization of the interior of Africa by European powers\nB. The expansion of the African diaspora to the New World\nC. The spread of Christianity into Sub-Saharan Africa\nD. The importation of New World products into Africa\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The passage by Walter Rodney emphasizes the exploitation of Africa through imperialism and capitalism, particularly focusing on the economic draining of the continent by Western European powers. This critique aligns most closely with the transatlantic slave trade, which forcibly displaced millions of Africans to the New World, fueling European economies while devastating African societies. This process significantly expanded between 1450 and 1750, making the African diaspora central to Rodney's argument.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 291,
        "output_tokens": 96,
        "total_tokens": 387
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
