      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}.\n\nThe Spanish insisted on control of the western hemisphere because they believed Portugal had not yet discovered or claimed the New World (e.g., the Americas), and they sought to secure their own exploration and colonization rights before Portugal could do so. This was a strategic move to prevent Portuguese expansion into territories they believed were still unclaimed. The treaty was not primarily about converting Barbary states or protecting Native states, nor was it about India.",
