      "generated_answer": "The passage describes how economic necessity led women to enter public life, including working and eating in public unescorted, marking a shift in gender roles and social norms. This change is most directly tied to the expanding rights and public participation of women, culminating in their right to vote. Therefore, the scenario best aligns with the **19th Amendment**, which granted women the right to vote in 1920.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
