  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_history_4626",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This question refers to the following information.\n[T]he the end and measure of this power, when in every man's hands in the state of nature, being the preservation of all of his society, that is, all mankind in general, it can have no other end or measure, when in the hands of the magistrate, but to preserve the members of that society in their lives, liberties, and possessions, and so cannot be an absolute, arbitrary power over their lives and fortunes, which are as much as possible to be preserved, but a power to make law, and annex such penalties to them, as may tend to the preservation of the whole by cutting off those parts, and those only, which are so corrupt that they threaten the sound and healthy, without which no severity is lawful. And this power has its original only from compact, and agreement, and the mutual consent of those who make up the community. …\nWhensoever, therefore, the legislative shall transgress this fundamental rule of society; and either by ambition, fear, folly or corruption, endeavor to grasp themselves, or put into the hands of any other, an absolute power over the lives, liberties, and estates of the people; by this breach of trust they forfeit the power the people had put into their hands for quite contrary ends.\nJohn Locke, Second Treatise of Government, 1690\nFrom the passage, one may infer that Locke believed a government loses its legitimacy when\n\nOptions: \nA. when the people wish to change governors\nB. it does not have penalties for breaking the law\nC. it tries to exercise absolute power\nD. it does not have a legislative body\nE. it does not enact laws\nF. it is weak and can be overthrown\nG. the people do not follow the laws\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Locke argues that government power is derived from the people and must be used to preserve their lives, liberties, and property—not as an absolute, arbitrary force. He states that when the legislative body attempts to seize \"an absolute power over the lives, liberties, and estates of the people,\" it breaches the trust of the social contract and forfeits its authority. Therefore, the government loses legitimacy precisely when it tries to exercise absolute power.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 432,
        "output_tokens": 92,
        "total_tokens": 524
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
    },
    "cost": 3.9871999999999994e-05,
    "accuracy": 1.0,
    "for_optimality": false
  },
  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_history_4627",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This question refers to the following information.\nRead the following letter.\nIt happened . . . that a Spaniard saw an Indian . . . eating a piece of flesh taken from the body of an Indian who had been killed. . . . I had the culprit burned, explaining that the cause was his having killed that Indian and eaten him[,] which was prohibited by Your Majesty, and by me in Your Royal name. I further made the chief understand that all the people . . . must abstain from this custom. . . . I came . . . to protect their lives as well as their property, and to teach them that they were to adore but one God[,] . . . that they must turn from their idols, and the rites they had practiced until then, for these were lies and deceptions which the devil . . . had invented. . . . I, likewise, had come to teach them that Your Majesty, by the will of Divine Providence, rules the universe, and that they also must submit themselves to the imperial yoke, and do all that we who are Your Majesty's ministers here might order them.\n—Hernan Cortez, Fifth Letter to Holy Roman Emperor Charles V, 1521\nWhich of the following was NOT a result of the European conquest of the Americas realized by the end of the seventeenth century?\n\nOptions: \nA. Europeans established overseas colonies on the coasts of the Americas and throughout the continent of Africa.\nB. Europeans established colonies throughout Asia and the Pacific Islands.\nC. Europeans created vast global trade networks that allowed them to gain large accumulations of wealth.\nD. European conquest led to the extinction of the majority of plant and animal species in the Americas.\nE. Europeans expanded the African slave trade in response to the establishment of a plantation economy in the Americas and to demographic catastrophes among indigenous peoples.\nF. The European conquest resulted in a globally unified political system under European rule.\nG. The conquest resulted in a decrease in Europe's population.\nH. Europe's colonial expansion led to a global exchange of goods, flora, fauna, cultural practices, and diseases.\nI. The indigenous people of the Americas were able to retain their territories and political power.\nJ. Europeans were able to completely eliminate all native cultures and languages in the Americas.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The letter from Hernan Cortes highlights Spanish efforts to impose religious, political, and cultural control over Indigenous peoples, reflecting the broader impacts of European conquest. By the end of the seventeenth century, while European colonization caused massive cultural disruption, population decline, and forced labor systems, it did **not** result in the complete elimination of all native cultures and languages (some survived despite oppression), nor did it lead to a globally unified political system under European rule or the extinction of most plant and animal species in the Americas. However, the **most clearly false** statement is that indigenous peoples retained their territories and political power, which contradicts historical outcomes.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
      "success": true,
