      "generated_answer": "The Second Bank of the United States was established in 1816, primarily to address the fiscal instability and unregulated state banking that followed the War of 1812. The federal government needed a way to manage war debts, regulate currency, and restore financial order after the war. Therefore, the most direct cause was unregulated currency and federal debts after the War of 1812.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
