      "generated_answer": "The first passage, written by British journalist William Howard Russell, emphasizes the shock and outrage at the idea of a \"subject race\" rising against their masters, highlighting the racial hierarchy and the perceived unnaturalness of colonized people killing their colonizers. It frames the violence as a profound betrayal, rooted in racial and imperial superiority, where the victims were \"helpless ladies and children\" and the perpetrators were black men who dared to rebel. This aligns most closely with a sense of racial betrayal.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
