      "generated_answer": "The boycott of foreign cloth emphasized by Gandhi was most significantly assisted by the Great Depression, which began in 1929, as it severely disrupted global trade and made imported goods more expensive and less available, thus boosting indigenous production.\n\nThis economic shift increased reliance on local industries and swadeshi goods, aligning with Gandhi’s call for self-reliance and strengthening the boycott movement.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
