      "generated_answer": "G. An embodiment of the ideals of the Abolitionist movement.\n\nWilliam Lloyd Garrison was a leading abolitionist who used The Liberator to advocate for the immediate emancipation of enslaved people and equal rights for free Black Americans. The passage directly calls for the recognition of citizenship and rights for free colored persons, aligning clearly with abolitionist principles.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
