      "generated_answer": "The question asks which measure by Robespierre during the radical phase of the French Revolution was LEAST beneficial to the defense of France. While many of these policies—such as conscription (J), merit-based promotion (G), and rationing (H)—directly strengthened France’s military and internal stability, promoting a new Republican Calendar (I) was largely symbolic and had no practical military benefit. It distracted from wartime priorities and did not contribute to national defense, making it the least beneficial among the options.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
