    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-30b-a3b-instruct-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Depth First Search (DFS) can get stuck in a blind alley because it explores one path as deeply as possible before backtracking, and if that path leads to a dead end (blind alley) without a way forward, it may not efficiently return to explore other potential paths unless explicitly designed to handle it.\n\nAmong the options, BFS, A*, and Bidirectional Search are generally designed to avoid or efficiently handle such issues by exploring multiple paths or using heuristics.\n\nThus, the most likely technique to get stuck in a blind alley is Depth First Search.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 103,
        "output_tokens": 117,
        "total_tokens": 220
      },
