    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nimport heapq\n\ndef main():\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    # Parse first line\n    idx = 0\n    N = int(data[idx])\n    M = int(data[idx + 1])\n    idx += 2\n    \n    # Initialize Union-Find data structure\n    parent = list(range(N + 1))\n    rank = [0] * (N + 1)\n    \n    def find(x):\n        if parent[x] != x:\n            parent[x] = find(parent[x])\n        return parent[x]\n    \n    def union(x, y):\n        px, py = find(x), find(y)\n        if px == py:\n            return False\n        if rank[px] < rank[py]:\n            px, py = py, px\n        parent[py] = px\n        if rank[px] == rank[py]:\n            rank[px] += 1\n        return True\n    \n    # List to store all edges\n    edges = []\n    \n    # Process each operation\n    for _ in range(M):\n        K = int(data[idx])\n        C = int(data[idx + 1])\n        idx += 2\n        vertices = list(map(int, data[idx:idx + K]))\n        idx += K\n        \n        # Add edges between every pair of vertices in the subset\n        for i in range(len(vertices)):\n            for j in range(i + 1, len(vertices)):\n                u, v = vertices[i], vertices[j]\n                edges.append((C, u, v))\n    \n    # Sort edges by weight for Kruskal's algorithm\n    edges.sort()\n    \n    # Run Kruskal's algorithm to build MST\n    total_weight = 0\n    edges_used = 0\n    \n    for weight, u, v in edges:\n        if union(u, v):\n            total_weight += weight\n            edges_used += 1\n            if edges_used == N - 1:\n                break\n    \n    # Check if graph is connected (N-1 edges in MST)\n    if edges_used != N - 1:\n        print(-1)\n    else:\n        print(total_weight)\n\n# Call the function\nmain()\n```",
