      "generated_answer": "Here's the Python function body for the given problem:\n\n```python\nMOD = 10**9 + 7\n\ndef sum_of_group_powers(nums):\n    n = len(nums)\n    total = 0\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        max_val = nums[i]\n        min_val = nums[i]\n        for j in range(i, n):\n            current_val = nums[j]\n            if current_val > max_val:\n                max_val = current_val\n            if current_val < min_val:\n                min_val = current_val\n            power = max_val ** 2 * min_val\n            total = (total + power) % MOD\n\n    return total\n```\n\nThis function calculates the sum of the power of all non-empty groups of heroes by:\n1. Iterating through all possible starting indices of groups\n2. For each starting index, expanding the group to include all subsequent elements\n3. For each group, finding the maximum and minimum values\n4. Calculating the power as max² × min\n5. Adding this to the total sum while keeping it modulo 10⁹ + 7\n6. Returning the final result\n\nThe function handles the constraints efficiently by processing each possible group in O(n²) time, which is feasible for the given constraints (n ≤ 10⁵) with some optimizations (though this implementation is straightforward). For very large inputs, a more optimized approach would be needed.",
