      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef maxSumOfSquares(nums, k):\n    MOD = 10**9 + 7\n    \n    # Count the number of 1s in each bit position across all numbers\n    bit_count = [0] * 32  # Since numbers are up to 10^9, 32 bits is enough\n    \n    for num in nums:\n        for i in range(32):\n            if num & (1 << i):\n                bit_count[i] += 1\n    \n    # Reconstruct the maximum possible numbers using the available bits\n    # We want to maximize the sum of squares, so we should prefer larger numbers\n    # Strategy: For each bit position, try to assign 1s to the largest possible numbers\n    # We can create at most len(nums) numbers, but we only need k largest ones\n    \n    # Create k numbers using the bit_count\n    result_numbers = []\n    \n    # We'll create k numbers, starting from the highest bit\n    for _ in range(k):\n        num = 0\n        for i in range(31, -1, -1):\n            if bit_count[i] > 0:\n                num |= (1 << i)\n                bit_count[i] -= 1\n        result_numbers.append(num)\n    \n    # Calculate sum of squares\n    total = 0\n    for num in result_numbers:\n        total = (total + (num * num) % MOD) % MOD\n    \n    return total\n```",
