      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef maxFrequencyScore(nums, k):\n    nums.sort()\n    n = len(nums)\n    max_score = 1\n    \n    # Use sliding window with median optimization\n    left = 0\n    # We'll calculate the cost to make all elements in window equal to the median\n    # For odd length, median is the middle; for even, we can use left median or right median\n    # But we'll use the approach of minimizing cost by adjusting window\n    \n    # We'll use the fact that for minimum cost to make all elements equal,\n    # the target should be the median of the window.\n    # We'll use prefix sum to compute cost efficiently\n    \n    prefix_sum = [0]\n    for num in nums:\n        prefix_sum.append(prefix_sum[-1] + num)\n    \n    # Try all possible window lengths\n    for right in range(n):\n        # For current window [left, right], find the minimum cost to make all elements equal\n        # The optimal target is the median of the window\n        \n        # Calculate median index\n        mid = (left + right) // 2\n        median = nums[mid]\n        \n        # Calculate cost to make all elements in window equal to median\n        # Left part: elements from left to mid-1 need to be increased to median\n        # Right part: elements from mid+1 to right need to be decreased to median\n        \n        # Left cost: sum of (median - nums[i]) for i from left to mid-1\n        left_cost = 0\n        if mid > left:\n            left_cost = median * (mid - left) - (prefix_sum[mid] - prefix_sum[left])\n        \n        # Right cost: sum of (nums[i] - median) for i from mid+1 to right\n        right_cost = 0\n        if mid < right:\n            right_cost = (prefix_sum[right + 1] - prefix_sum[mid + 1]) - median * (right - mid)\n        \n        total_cost = left_cost + right_cost\n        \n        # If cost is within k, update max_score\n        while total_cost > k:\n            left += 1\n            # Recalculate median and cost for new window\n            if left > right:\n                break\n            mid = (left + right) // 2\n            median = nums[mid]\n            left_cost = 0\n            if mid > left:\n                left_cost = median * (mid - left) - (prefix_sum[mid] - prefix_sum[left])\n            right_cost = 0\n            if mid < right:\n                right_cost = (prefix_sum[right + 1] - prefix_sum[mid + 1]) - median * (right - mid)\n            total_cost = left_cost + right_cost\n        \n        # Update maximum score (window size)\n        if left <= right:\n            max_score = max(max_score, right - left + 1)\n    \n    return max_score\n```",
