ices:\n                        connected_indices.add(neighbor_idx)\n                        queue.append(neighbor_idx)\n\n    # Check if all indices are connected\n    return len(connected_indices) == len(nums)\n```\n\nThis function works by:\n1. Grouping indices by their prime factors (since GCD > 1 implies they share at least one prime factor)\n2. Using BFS to explore all indices connected through shared prime factors\n3. Verifying if all indices are reachable from any starting index\n\nThe key insight is that two indices are connected if they share at least one prime factor, which forms the basis of the graph connectivity check. The function returns True only if all indices are part of a single connected component.",
