      "generated_answer": "To find \\( P(D \\mid TP) \\), use Bayes' theorem:\n\n\\[\nP(D \\mid TP) = \\frac{P(TP \\mid D) \\cdot P(D)}{P(TP)}\n\\]\n\nGiven:\n- \\( P(D) = 0.05 \\),\n- \\( P(TP \\mid D) = 0.99 \\),\n- \\( P(\\neg D) = 0.95 \\),\n- \\( P(\\neg TP \\mid \\neg D) = 0.97 \\Rightarrow P(TP \\mid \\neg D) = 0.03 \\).\n\nThen:\n\\[\nP(TP) = P(TP \\mid D)P(D) + P(TP \\mid \\neg D)P(\\neg D) = 0.99 \\cdot 0.05 + 0.03 \\cdot 0.95 = 0.0495 + 0.0285 = 0.078.\n\\]\n\nThus:\n\\[\nP(D \\mid TP) = \\frac{0.99 \\cdot 0.05}{0.078} \\approx 0.635.\n\\]\n\nThe correct choice is \\(\\boxed{F}\\).",
