    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_503",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose a stock has the following information. It is listed on the London stock exchange and operates throughout Europe. The yield on a UK 10 year treasury is 2.8%. The stock in question will earn 8.6% as per historical data. The Beta for the stock is 1.4, i.e., it is 140% volatile to the changes in the general stock market. What is the expected rate of return?\n\nOptions: \nA. 5.6\nB. 2.8\nC. 1.4\nD. 10.92\nE. 7.98\nF. 6.2\nG. 9.4\nH. 8.6\nI. 11.76\nJ. 12.34\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "mistralai/ministral-3b-2512",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct approach uses the **Capital Asset Pricing Model (CAPM)** to estimate the expected return:\n\n\\[\nE(R) = R_f + \\beta (E(R_m) - R_f)\n\\]\n\nGiven the UK 10Y Treasury yield (\\(R_f\\)) is **2.8%** and the stock’s **historical yield (8.6%)** likely reflects \\(E(R_m) - R_f\\) (market premium), the expected return is:\n\n\\[\nE(R) = 2.8\\% + 1.4 \\times 8.6\\% = 2.8\\% + 12.04\\% = 14.84\\% \\quad (\\text{Not listed})\n\\]\n\nSince none of the options match this, the closest plausible interpretation (assuming \\(8.6\\%\\) is the **market return** rather than the premium) yields:\n\n\\[\nE(R) = 2.8\\% + 1.4 \\times (8.6\\% - 2.8\\%) = 2.8\\% + 9.4\\% = 12.2\\% \\approx \\boxed{J}\n\\]\n\n*(Note: The exact calculation depends on whether \\(8.6\\%\\) is the market return or the premium; \\(J\\) is the closest match.)*",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 233,
        "output_tokens": 269,
        "total_tokens": 502
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
