  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_784",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Assuming that each lived for the term of the policy, compare the cost of a $5,000 20-payment life insurance policy for a young man 25 years of age with a man 45 years of age.\n\nOptions: \nA. $3649 and $2207\nB. $2207 and $5000\nC. $110.35 and $182.45\nD. $5000 and $5000\nE. $1500 and $2500\nF. $182.45 and $110.35\nG. $4250 and $6250\nH. $2207 and $3649\nI. $3649 and $3649\nJ. $2500 and $4500\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-30b-a3b-instruct-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The cost of a life insurance policy increases with age due to higher risk. A 25-year-old is healthier and poses less risk than a 45-year-old, so their premiums are lower. Therefore, the younger man’s premium should be less than the older man’s, which matches option F: $182.45 and $110.35 — but this is reversed.\n\nWait, option F lists $182.45 (older) and $110.35 (younger), which is incorrect because the older man should pay more.\n\nCorrectly, the 25-year-old should have a lower premium than the 45-year-old. Looking at the options, option H: $2207 and $3649 is incorrect in order. Option A: $3649 and $2207 implies the 25-year-old pays more — also wrong.\n\nWait — the only option with the younger man paying less is F: $182.45 (25) and $110.35 (45)? That can’t be — $110 is lower, meaning the 45-year-old pays less? No — the numbers must match the age.\n\nWait, let’s re-express: better premium for younger person.\n\nSo, correct order: 25-year-old (lower) → 45-year-old (higher).\n\nOnly option F has lower number first: $182.45 and $110.35 — but that would mean 25-year-old pays $182.45, 45-year-old pays $110.35 — which is backwards.\n\nAh — none seem correct? Wait — option C: $110.35 and $182.45 — so 25-year-old pays $110.35, 45-year-old pays $182.45 — that makes sense.\n\nYes — younger man pays less. So $110.35 for 25-year-old, $182.45 for 45-year-old.\n\nSo option C: $110.35 and $182.45 — correct order and logic.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 263,
        "output_tokens": 485,
        "total_tokens": 748
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
    },
    "cost": 0.00018109000000000002,
    "accuracy": 0.0,
    "for_optimality": true
  },
