      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **H. The money (or banking) multiplier**.\n\nIn banking systems, the money multiplier equals one when the reserve ratio is zero (no required reserves), as it represents the theoretical maximum expansion of the money supply per unit of reserves. Under typical conditions (with a reserve ratio \\( r \\)), the multiplier is \\( \\frac{1}{r} \\), but the *idealized* case where it equals one is conceptually central to the multiplier’s definition. None of the other options directly relate to the money multiplier’s fundamental property.",
