      "generated_answer": "The brother’s cutting of timber on the section suitable for cultivation is not wasteful because that land is more valuable for cultivation than for timber. Since he is only removing timber to prepare the land for crop production, his actions are consistent with improving the land’s utility, which aligns with ameliorative waste—actions that enhance the value of the property. Thus, the correct answer is D.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
