      "generated_answer": "The approach used by Albrecht and Axell is known as the search-theoretic model of the labor market, which incorporates heterogeneous sellers (workers) with different reservation wages. This model assumes that workers differ in their willingness to accept jobs, leading to a distribution of reservation prices. The most common answer to this question is **search-theoretic model**.\n\n\\boxed{\\text{search-theoretic model}}",
