    "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This approach was used by Albrecht and Axell to develop a model that assumes two types of sellers with different reservation prices.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "mistralai/ministral-3b-2512",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{\\text{The **Stackelberg model with asymmetric information (or \"two-seller model\") in the context of price competition under imperfect information, often framed as a \"two-stage game\" where the \"leader\" (higher-reservation-price seller) sets price first, followed by the \"follower\" (lower-reservation-price seller).}}\n\nThis model is rooted in **Albrecht & Axell (1979)**, where they analyzed **price-setting duopoly with asymmetric reservation prices**, emphasizing strategic interactions where the dominant seller (higher reservation price) sets a higher price, leading to a **second-best outcome** due to incomplete information. The framework extends to **market structure analysis** (e.g., monopolistic competition with asymmetric sellers).",
      "success": true,
