    "global index": "QANTA_Social Science_2",
    "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An injunctive message can block a negative outcome of this process through the \"boomerang effect.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-30b-a3b-instruct-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "An injunctive message can block a negative outcome of this process through the \"boomerang effect\" by reinforcing positive behaviors and discouraging counterproductive ones. The \"boomerang effect\" occurs when a message intended to persuade produces the opposite effect, so a well-crafted injunctive message can redirect attitudes or actions to avoid such backlash. The correct answer is \\boxed{behavior}.\n\nExplanation: Injunctive messages influence what people believe they should do, and when used effectively, they can prevent the boomerang effect by aligning norms with desired behavior. Without such alignment, the message may backfire, leading to resistance or contrary actions. Thus, behavior is the key target of such interventions.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 80,
        "output_tokens": 145,
        "total_tokens": 225
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
