    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We analyze the recursive function $ f(i, j) $ defined modulo 5. For $ i = 0 $, $ f(0, j) = \\text{mod}_5(j+1) $, so $ f(0,0)=1 $, $ f(0,1)=2 $, ..., $ f(0,4)=0 $. For $ i \\geq 1 $ and $ j = 0 $, $ f(i,0) = f(i-1,1) $. For $ j \\geq 1 $, $ f(i,j) = f(i-1, f(i,j-1)) $. By computing small values, we find that $ f(1,j) $ cycles every 5 steps and $ f(2,j) $ stabilizes to a constant pattern due to the modulo 5 constraints. After observing patterns, we find that $ f(i,2) $ becomes constant for $ i \\geq 3 $, and in fact $ f(i,2) = 3 $ for all $ i \\geq 3 $. Since $ 2015 \\geq 3 $, we conclude $ f(2015,2) = 3 $.\n\n\\boxed{3}",
