    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: It is possible to produce very high magnetic fields over small volumes by special techniques. What would be the resonance frequency of an electron spin in an organic radical in a field of $1.0 \\mathrm{{kT}}$ ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 3.2 $10^{{13}} \\mathrm{{~Hz}}$\nB. 1.8 $10^{{13}} \\mathrm{{~Hz}}$\nC. 4.0 $10^{{13}} \\mathrm{{~Hz}}$\nD. 3.0 $10^{{12}} \\mathrm{{~Hz}}$\nE. 5.5 $10^{{13}} \\mathrm{{~Hz}}$\nF.  2.8 $10^{{13}} \\mathrm{{~Hz}}$\nG. 1.5 $10^{{13}} \\mathrm{{~Hz}}$\nH. 3.6 $10^{{13}} \\mathrm{{~Hz}}$\nI. 2.2 $10^{{13}} \\mathrm{{~Hz}}$\nJ. 2.5 $10^{{13}} \\mathrm{{~Hz}}$\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-30b-a3b-instruct-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The resonance frequency of an electron spin in a magnetic field is given by the EPR (electron paramagnetic resonance) equation: $ f = \\frac{g \\mu_B B}{h} $, where $ g \\approx 2 $ for organic radicals, $ \\mu_B = 9.274 \\times 10^{-24} \\, \\mathrm{erg/G} $, $ B = 1.0 \\, \\mathrm{kT} = 10,000 \\, \\mathrm{T} $, and $ h = 6.626 \\times 10^{-27} \\, \\mathrm{erg \\cdot s} $. Plugging in the values:  \n$ f \\approx \\frac{2 \\times 9.274 \\times 10^{-24} \\times 10^4}{6.626 \\times 10^{-27}} \\approx 2.8 \\times 10^{13} \\, \\mathrm{Hz} $.  \nThis matches option F.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
