    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The observed Kα lines at 0.7092 Å and 1.6578 Å suggest elements with atomic numbers near copper (Z = 29). Using Moseley’s law, which relates the square root of the frequency of Kα lines to atomic number, we can estimate the atomic numbers: 0.7092 Å corresponds to Z ≈ 44 (Ruthenium), but this does not match closely. Recalculating carefully, 0.7092 Å is close to the Kα of molybdenum (Z=42, λ ≈ 0.710 Å), and 1.6578 Å is near nickel (Z=28, λ ≈ 1.66 Å). Thus, the impurities are molybdenum and nickel.\n\nThe correct answer is:  \n\\boxed{E}",
