    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To solve this, we use the principle of buoyancy and the given specific gravity (SG = 2/3). When the log floats horizontally, the submerged volume equals the weight of displaced water. As length decreases, the log eventually floats vertically when the submerged length equals the diameter.\n\nThe critical ratio occurs when the submerged length equals the diameter, so the volume of displaced water equals the cross-sectional area times the diameter. Using SG = ρ_log/ρ_water = 2/3, we derive the diameter-to-length ratio as \\( \\frac{3}{2} = 1.5 \\).\n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{A}\\).",
