    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10309",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the solution for the equationX=AX+bu;X(0) = X_0 where A=\\vert10\\vert,b=\\vert1\\vert,X_0 =\\vert- 1\\vert, \\vert- 22\\vert\\vert2\\vert\\vert0\\vert u(t) = \\delta(t) (impulse function).\n\nOptions: \nA. -3\nB. 2\nC. 0\nD. 3\nE. 10\nF. -2\nG. 22\nH. 1\nI. -10\nJ. -1\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-30b-a3b-instruct-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The given equation is a linear time-invariant system: $ X = AX + bu $ with initial condition $ X(0) = X_0 $, and input $ u(t) = \\delta(t) $, the Dirac impulse. For such systems, the solution at $ t = 0^+ $ is $ X(0^+) = X_0 + b \\cdot u(0) $, and since $ u(t) = \\delta(t) $, the impulse contributes $ b \\cdot 1 $ to the state. Given $ X_0 = \\begin{bmatrix} -1 \\\\ 0 \\end{bmatrix} $, $ b = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 \\\\ 2 \\end{bmatrix} $, the total state jump at $ t = 0 $ is $ \\begin{bmatrix} -1 \\\\ 0 \\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix} 1 \\\\ 2 \\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix} 0 \\\\ 2 \\end{bmatrix} $. Since the question appears to ask for a scalar value and likely refers to the first state component (which is 0), the answer is C. 0.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
