    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The power received by a dipole antenna in free space can be calculated using the Friis transmission equation:  \n$ P_r = P_t G_t G_r \\left( \\frac{\\lambda}{4\\pi d} \\right)^2 $,  \nwhere $ P_t = 1 $ kW, $ d = 500 $ km, $ f = 200 $ MHz → $ \\lambda = c/f = 1.5 $ m, and for a half-wave dipole, $ G_t = G_r = 1.64 $.  \nPlugging in: $ P_r = 1000 \\times 1.64 \\times 1.64 \\times \\left( \\frac{1.5}{4\\pi \\times 500 \\times 10^3} \\right)^2 \\approx 1.03 \\times 10^{-10} $ W.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
