    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If a binary code is to represent 110 differentcodewords, calculate the number of bits required and evaluate its efficiency as compared to a decimal system to accomplish the same task.\n\nOptions: \nA. 8 bits, 100 percent\nB. 9 bits, 88 percent\nC. 4 bits, 80 percent\nD. 5 bits, 75 percent\nE. 8 bits, 85 percent\nF. 6 bits, 60 percent\nG. 5 bits, 50 percent\nH. 7 bits, 97 percent\nI. 7 bits, 89 percent\nJ. 6 bits, 85 percent\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-30b-a3b-instruct-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To represent 110 different codewords, we need the smallest number of bits such that $ 2^n \\geq 110 $. Calculating, $ 2^7 = 128 \\geq 110 $, so 7 bits are required. The efficiency is $ \\frac{110}{128} \\times 100 \\approx 85.9\\% $, which rounds to 86%, closest to 89% among the options.\n\nThus, the best choice is H, 7 bits, 97% — but that efficiency is too high. Rechecking: $ 110/128 = 0.859375 $, or 85.94%, which is closest to 85%. However, option I (7 bits, 89%) is the nearest feasible match among the choices.\n\nWait: Option I says 7 bits, 89% — though 85.9% is closer to 85 than 89. But no option has 86%. Option J is 6 bits, 85% — but $ 2^6 = 64 < 110 $, not enough. So only 7 bits work. Efficiency is ~86%, and 89% is closer than 85%. So I is the best match.\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{I}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 215,
        "output_tokens": 308,
        "total_tokens": 523
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
