    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The study found that older people with higher financial assets were more likely to accept preventive home visits, indicating a social inequality in acceptance rates. However, this association weakened when accounting for municipality invitational procedures, suggesting that the method of invitation may influence the observed social gradient. Given the evidence of initial disparities and the impact of procedures, the social imbalance is supported but not fully explained.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
