    "global index": "MMLUPro_history_4645",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This question refers to the following information.\n\"We found that not only was it a civil war, an effort by a people who had for years been seeking their liberation from any colonial influence whatsoever, but also we found that the Vietnamese whom we had enthusiastically molded after our own image were hard put to take up the fight against the threat we were supposedly saving them from.\n\"We found most people didn't even know the difference between communism and democracy. They only wanted to work in rice paddies without helicopters strafing them and bombs with napalm burning their villages and tearing their country apart. They wanted everything to do with the war, particularly with this foreign presence of the United States of America, to leave them alone in peace, and they practiced the art of survival by siding with whichever military force was present at a particular time, be it Viet Cong, North Vietnamese or American.\"\nJohn Kerry, 1971\nThe most important factor in the defeat of Democratic presidential candidates in the elections of 1952 and 1968 was\n\nOptions: \nA. the candidates' lack of military service records\nB. the rise of third-party candidates that split the Democratic vote\nC. the American public's desire to avoid conflict and return to a more conservative political and social life\nD. the Democratic Party's perceived weakness on national security issues\nE. the Democratic candidates' controversial positions on civil rights legislation\nF. the Democratic candidates' inability to effectively communicate their policies to the public\nG. the Democratic Party's unequivocal support of the Equal Rights Amendment\nH. the Democratic Party platform pledge to increase taxes in order to pay off the national debt\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The passage by John Kerry highlights growing disillusionment with U.S. involvement in Vietnam and skepticism about the rationale for the war, reflecting broader concerns about national security and foreign policy during the Cold War era. This public doubt contributed to the perception that the Democratic Party was weak on national defense, especially in 1952 (after the Korean War) and in 1968 (during the Vietnam War). Thus, the most accurate answer is:\n\n\\boxed{D}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 399,
        "output_tokens": 97,
        "total_tokens": 496
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
    },
    "cost": 3.8029e-05,
    "accuracy": 0.0,
    "for_optimality": true
  },
  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_history_4645",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This question refers to the following information.\n\"We found that not only was it a civil war, an effort by a people who had for years been seeking their liberation from any colonial influence whatsoever, but also we found that the Vietnamese whom we had enthusiastically molded after our own image were hard put to take up the fight against the threat we were supposedly saving them from.\n\"We found most people didn't even know the difference between communism and democracy. They only wanted to work in rice paddies without helicopters strafing them and bombs with napalm burning their villages and tearing their country apart. They wanted everything to do with the war, particularly with this foreign presence of the United States of America, to leave them alone in peace, and they practiced the art of survival by siding with whichever military force was present at a particular time, be it Viet Cong, North Vietnamese or American.\"\nJohn Kerry, 1971\nThe most important factor in the defeat of Democratic presidential candidates in the elections of 1952 and 1968 was\n\nOptions: \nA. the candidates' lack of military service records\nB. the rise of third-party candidates that split the Democratic vote\nC. the American public's desire to avoid conflict and return to a more conservative political and social life\nD. the Democratic Party's perceived weakness on national security issues\nE. the Democratic candidates' controversial positions on civil rights legislation\nF. the Democratic candidates' inability to effectively communicate their policies to the public\nG. the Democratic Party's unequivocal support of the Equal Rights Amendment\nH. the Democratic Party platform pledge to increase taxes in order to pay off the national debt\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-30b-a3b-instruct-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The most important factor in the defeat of Democratic presidential candidates in 1952 and 1968 was the public's growing desire to avoid conflict and return to a more conservative political and social life, especially in the context of the Vietnam War and perceived liberal activism. In 1952, Dwight Eisenhower capitalized on discontent with war and government spending, while in 1968, the split within the Democratic Party and the appeal of a “law and order” message resonated with voters weary of social unrest and war. Thus, option C best captures the broader public mood driving these election outcomes.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 399,
        "output_tokens": 131,
        "total_tokens": 530
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
    },
    "cost": 7.515000000000001e-05,
    "accuracy": 1.0,
    "for_optimality": true
  },
  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_history_4654",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This question refers to the following information.\n\"The question as to who, and what, is responsible for African underdevelopment can be answered at two levels. Firstly, the answer is that the operation of the imperialist system bears major responsibility for African economic retardation by draining African wealth and by making it impossible to develop more rapidly the resources of the continent. Secondly, one has to deal with those who manipulate the system and those who are either agents or unwitting accomplices of the said system. The capitalists of Western Europe were the ones who actively extended their exploitation from inside Europe to cover the whole of Africa.\"\nWalter Rodney, historian, How Europe Underdeveloped Africa, 1974\nWhich of the following best explains the importance of trading contacts with Europeans for Sub-Saharan Africans in the period 1450 to 1750 C.E.?\n\nOptions: \nA. Sub-Saharan Africans consolidated new states and kingdoms by trading with the Europeans for firearms.\nB. Sub-Saharan Africans relied on trading contacts with Europeans to circumvent the Arab slave trade.\nC. Sub-Saharan Africans depended on European merchants as the sole purchasers of slaves.\nD. Sub-Saharan Africans established significant economic advantage by trading indigenous resources for European goods.\nE. Sub-Saharan Africans developed a dependency on European goods, leading to a collapse of local industries.\nF. Sub-Saharan Africans used European trading contacts to gain access to European education and religion.\nG. Sub-Saharan Africans relied on European merchants to sustain population growth through the constant importation of New World foodstuffs.\nH. Sub-Saharan Africans allied with European powers to evict Muslim and Arab merchant princes from encroaching on their sovereignty.\nI. Sub-Saharan Africans utilized trading contacts with Europeans to spread their cultural influence throughout Europe.\nJ. Sub-Saharan Africans engaged in trade with Europeans to acquire new agricultural techniques.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-30b-a3b-instruct-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The passage by Walter Rodney emphasizes how European imperialism and capitalist exploitation drained African wealth and hindered development. During 1450–1750, European demand for slaves and African resources distorted local economies, encouraging internal conflicts and reinforcing dependency on external trade rather than self-sustained development. Option E best reflects this dynamic, as African societies became dependent on European goods, undermining local industries and contributing to long-term underdevelopment.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 432,
        "output_tokens": 93,
        "total_tokens": 525
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
    },
    "cost": 6.525e-05,
    "accuracy": 0.0,
    "for_optimality": true
  },
