      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{J}. \n\nCandide's repeated phrase \"everything happens for the best\" reflects the philosophical optimism of Leibniz, who argued that we live in the \"best of all possible worlds\" due to a pre-established, divinely ordained order—implying the universe is predetermined. This aligns with option J, which emphasizes a pre-determined and unchangeable system, a view Voltaire satirizes throughout the novel.",
